    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0612" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6852: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-01T18:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 2—11:57 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>141. Agreement referred to in my telegram 137, April 30, 5 p.m., has been signed.
                    Terms practically as summarized in my telegram 119, April 21, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>Large labor day parade this morning but no disorder.</p>
                <pb facs="0613" n="513" xml:id="pg513"/>
                <p>Russian press reports that Japanese Diplomatic Agent Matsudaira stated that
                    Japanese Siberian policy is not independent but is fully in accord with other
                    Allies. Denial of accuracy of this statement by Matsudaira or representatives
                    Allies has been expected by Russians but has not so far appeared, which causes
                    considerable comment. Repeated to Peking and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
